STATEMENT: >>>
Grammar to load: `tree-sitter-grammars.tree-sitter-javascript` (nixpkgs, 0.25.0, `python313Packages`/`python314Packages` binding present).

Candidate items (node type, confirmed against upstream `tree-sitter/tree-sitter-javascript`'s `src/node-types.json`): `class_declaration`, `function_declaration`, `method_definition`, `arrow_function`, `export_statement` — largely the same names TypeScript's grammar uses for the shapes both languages share.

Present in this repo today: 7 files under `docs/sdoc/board/assets/` (`app.js`, `board.js`, `card.js`, `grammars.js`, `layout.js`, `perspective.js`, `plan.js` — the whiteboard-view board app, loaded by `docs/sdoc/board/index.html`), plus 2 `.mjs` update scripts, `overlays/claude-code/{census,locate}.mjs`.

Gap: deprioritized. Per the operator, the board app's `.js` is a rewrite target for modern TS (see WORK-LANG-TYPESCRIPT), so this language's extractor support should not be built out as a separate long-lived surface — if anything is built, it should be built to converge on the TypeScript grammar's node types (see the shared node-type names above) so the same item queries survive the rewrite.
